## 2. Boundary geometry — ODbL 1.0

`src/data/geo_jls.json`, `src/data/geo_counties.json`,
`src/data/geo_regions5.json` and `tools/pipeline/raw/jls_geo_osm.geojson` are
**derived databases** under the Open Database License 1.0
(https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/).

- `geo_jls.json` and `jls_geo_osm.geojson` derive from an Overpass
  `admin_level=7` extract of **OpenStreetMap**. © OpenStreetMap contributors.
- `geo_counties.json` and `geo_regions5.json` derive from **geoBoundaries**
  (ADM1, itself OSM-derived). © OpenStreetMap contributors.

Per ODbL §4.3 the source is attributed wherever these are displayed (the map
legend, the application footer, and both the PNG and SVG exports). Per §4.4,
any redistribution of these files or of a database derived from them must be
under ODbL 1.0 and must carry the same attribution.

## 3. Migration statistics — see source terms

- **2018 origin–destination flows** (`src/data/odm.json` 2018 layer,
  `src/data/jls_drill.json`, `tools/pipeline/ref/od2018.json`, and the measured
  layer of `geo_jls.json`): derived from Pitoski, Lampoltshammer & Parycek
  (2021), figshare 10.6084/m9.figshare.12497177, **CC BY 4.0**. Cite the paper.
- **All other years** in `odm.json` are IPF estimates computed here from the
  above structure and DZS margins. They are estimates, not measurements, and
  are labelled as such throughout the interface.
- **DZS series** (`src/data/atlas_data2.json`, `citizen.json`, `demo.json`):
  Državni zavod za statistiku, tables 7.4.1.–7.4.3. and STAN-2026-2-1
  (podaci.dzs.hr). Reused under DZS terms of use; attribute DZS.

## 4. Fonts — SIL Open Font License 1.1

`src/fonts/*.woff2` are the latin and latin-ext subsets Google Fonts serves for:

- **Oswald** — Copyright 2016 The Oswald Project Authors
  (https://github.com/googlefonts/OswaldFont)
- **IBM Plex Sans** and **IBM Plex Mono** — Copyright © 2017 IBM Corp. with
  Reserved Font Name "Plex"

Both are licensed under the **SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1**. OFL §2
requires the licence to travel with any copy of the font software, so the full
text ships in `public/fonts/OFL-Oswald.txt` and `public/fonts/OFL-IBMPlex.txt`
and is served by the built site at `./fonts/`. The fonts are self-hosted rather
than loaded from Google's CDN so that no visitor's IP reaches a third party on
first paint.

## 5. Exported figures — CC BY 4.0

The PNG and SVG a reader exports from the running atlas are **Produced Works**
in the sense of ODbL §4.3, not derived databases: they are renderings, so the
share-alike obligation in §4.4 does not reach them and their terms are ours to
set. They are published under **Creative Commons Attribution 4.0**
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/) — reuse them in a paper, a slide
or a report, keeping the credit band the export already prints, which carries
every upstream attribution the choice depends on (DZS, Pitoski et al. CC BY,
ODbL boundaries).

This does not extend to the underlying data: the IPF layers remain generated
output, not published statistics, and §3 above still governs the series.

## The atlas is non-commercial

It is published as a free, non-commercial project. Nothing it displays is
derived from the companion study's expression — the numbers are DZS's or
computed here, and what comes from the study is a threshold and a grouping,
which are method rather than text — so the study's NC clause is not engaged
either way. The statement is made so a reader does not have to reason it out.

## Note on the estimates

The IPF layers are generated output, not published statistics. Do not
redistribute them as DZS figures. `README.md` and `tools/pipeline/README.md`
document how they are produced.

## Note on the companion study

The atlas was built as an interactive companion to:

> Maras, M. i Vinovrški, L. (2026). Unutarnje i vanjske migracije stanovništva
> županija kao kriterij regionalizacije Hrvatske. *Elektronički zbornik radova
> Veleučilišta u Šibeniku*, 20(1–2), 59–76.
> <https://hrcak.srce.hr/349820> · <https://doi.org/10.51650/ezrvs.20.1-2.4>

The paper is open access under **CC BY-NC**. Nothing from it is reproduced here —
no text, no table, no figure. Two methodological choices follow it, the
classification threshold and the five-region grouping, and both are marked
"iz rada" in the interface and credited to it; every number in the atlas comes
from the DZS series or is computed here, so the atlas is not a derivative of the
paper's content and the NC clause is not engaged by anything it displays.

This project is unaffiliated and unofficial. Its author has no connection to the
study's authors or their institutions, and they have neither reviewed nor
endorsed it. The citation lives in `src/lib/credits.ts`, which is what every
surface derives from.
